   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the banking law and the New York state urban development\ncorporation act, in relation to the capital access program",
    "basePrintNo": "S8094",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8094-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §212, Bank L; amd §16-k, UDC Act (as proposed in S.1690-A & A.6716-A)",
    "lawSection": "Banking Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8094\n\nSPONSOR: SANDERS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the banking law and the New York state urban development\ncorporation act, in relation to the capital access program\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis is a chapter amendment that makes changes to the provisions of\nL.2023 c.699, relating to the Pursuit lending corporation, to add clari-\nfying language, to remove the provisions requiring the development of a\nweb portal and third-party marketing, and other technical changes.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis legislation amends the underlying chapter by adding clarifying\nlanguage that the corporation mentioned in the statute is the New York\nbusiness development corporation, removes portions of the bill that\nrequire the creation of an integrated web portal and provide funding for\nmarketing to be directed to potential loan recipients and institutions.\n\nThis legislation also adds a section to the Urban Development Corpo-\nration Act to require the corporation and any contractors to work to\nincrease minority and women-owned businesses participation in the capi-\ntal access loan program.\n\n \nEXISTING LAW:\n\nNone.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation is a negotiated change to the underlying chapter.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter amendment to Chapter 699 of the Laws of 2023. S.1690-A and\nA.6716-A both passed the Senate and Assembly, respectfully, in June\n2023.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the same date and in the same manner as a\nchapter of the laws of 2023 amending the banking law and the New York\nstate urban development corporation act relating to the capital access\nprogram, as proposed in legislative bills numbers S.1690-A and A.6716-A,\ntakes effect.\n",
